        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "1. For vacation purposes only, a regular full time employee is defined as one who is regularly and continuously scheduled to work at least forty (40) hours a week:",
            "block_bbox": [
                49,
                100,
                536,
                155
            ],
            "block_id": 1,
            "block_order": 2,
            "group_id": 1,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    49.0,
                    100.0
                ],
                [
                    536.0,
                    100.0
                ],
                [
                    536.0,
                    155.0
                ],
                [
                    49.0,
                    155.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "a. For vacation purposes only, a regular part time employee is one who is regularly scheduled to work less than the normal work week (40 hours).",
            "block_bbox": [
                66,
                162,
                536,
                216
            ],
            "block_id": 2,
            "block_order": 3,
            "group_id": 2,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    66.0,
                    162.0
                ],
                [
                    536.0,
                    162.0
                ],
                [
                    536.0,
                    216.0
                ],
                [
                    66.0,
                    216.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "2. The “vacation period” shall be defined as that period beginning May 1 and ending on the Saturday nearest September 30, except that the third and fourth weeks vacation will be scheduled by the Company as business operations permit during the “vacation year”, i.e., May 1 through the following April 30.",
            "block_bbox": [
                49,
                223,
                536,
                311
            ],
            "block_id": 3,
            "block_order": 4,
            "group_id": 3,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    49.0,
                    223.0
                ],
                [
                    536.0,
                    223.0
                ],
                [
                    536.0,
                    311.0
                ],
                [
                    49.0,
                    311.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "3. Unused vacation grant may not be carried over to the following vacation year.",
            "block_bbox": [
                49,
                317,
                535,
                355
            ],
            "block_id": 4,
            "block_order": 5,
            "group_id": 4,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    49.0,
                    317.0
                ],
                [
                    535.0,
                    317.0
                ],
                [
                    535.0,
                    355.0
                ],
                [
                    49.0,
                    355.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "4. All vacation pay shall be calculated on the employee's basic straight-time hourly rate.",
            "block_bbox": [
                48,
                362,
                535,
                399
            ],
            "block_id": 5,
            "block_order": 6,
            "group_id": 5,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    48.0,
                    362.0
                ],
                [
                    535.0,
                    362.0
                ],
                [
                    535.0,
                    399.0
                ],
                [
                    48.0,
                    399.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "a. If an employee is regularly and continuously scheduled to work on a night shift for which a fixed night differential is paid, such differential shall be part of his basic hourly rate for the purpose of computing vacation pay. Night differential does not include premium overtime rate of pay.",
            "block_bbox": [
                65,
                406,
                536,
                494
            ],
            "block_id": 6,
            "block_order": 7,
            "group_id": 6,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    65.0,
                    406.0
                ],
                [
                    536.0,
                    406.0
                ],
                [
                    536.0,
                    494.0
                ],
                [
                    65.0,
                    494.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "5. Eligible employees who have changed from a part time to a regular full time basis, or vice versa, during the vacation year, will be entitled to a vacation grant consisting of the weekly credits earned for part time work and the monthly credits earned for full time work during such vacation year as described in Section 1.",
            "block_bbox": [
                47,
                500,
                535,
                602
            ],
            "block_id": 7,
            "block_order": 8,
            "group_id": 7,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    47.0,
                    500.0
                ],
                [
                    535.0,
                    500.0
                ],
                [
                    535.0,
                    602.0
                ],
                [
                    47.0,
                    602.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "6. Vacation selection will be granted on a seniority (length of continuous on-the-job service) basis, so far as possible, preference as to dates being given in the order of length of such service. Vacation schedules must be so arranged as not to interfere with the regular and efficient conduct of the business of the Company.",
            "block_bbox": [
                47,
                609,
                535,
                712
            ],
            "block_id": 8,
            "block_order": 9,
            "group_id": 8,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    47.0,
                    609.0
                ],
                [
                    535.0,
                    609.0
                ],
                [
                    535.0,
                    712.0
                ],
                [
                    47.0,
                    712.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "7. Unless the business of the Company directs otherwise, vacation grants up to and including two weeks will be taken in consecutive days within the vacation period.",
            "block_bbox": [
